---
// Mockup only: the condensed story under the demo (same in every option).
import Arena from './Arena.astro';
interface Props {
	scene: any;
}
const { scene } = Astro.props;
const live = scene.versions.filter((v: any) => v.live);
const cats = ['open', 'obstacles', 'scribbles', 'mixed', 'mazes', 'traps'];
const best = Object.fromEntries(cats.map((c) => [c, Math.max(...live.map((v: any) => v.test_success[c]))]));
---

<section class="story">
	<h2>How Wheely learned to drive</h2>
	<div class="cols">
		<div class="text">
			<p>
				Wheely gets five distance rays, the direction and distance to B, and what its wheels did a moment ago. A
				network of 350 numbers turns that into two wheel speeds, 15 times a second. It learned by trial and error
				(reinforcement learning) on thousands of random layouts. No layout here was in its training set.
			</p>
			<p>
				It took a few tries. The first versions found loopholes in the rewards I wrote, and the fixes taught me as
				much as the successes did.
			</p>
		</div>
		<table>
			<caption>Success on 1,000 unseen layouts per type</caption>
			<thead>
				<tr><th></th>{cats.map((c) => <th>{c}</th>)}</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				{
					live.map((v: any) => (
						<tr>
							<th>{v.name}</th>
							{cats.map((c) => (
								<td class:list={{ best: v.test_success[c] === best[c] }}>{Math.round(100 * v.test_success[c])}</td>
							))}
						</tr>
					))
				}
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>

	<h3>What went wrong along the way</h3>
	<div class="fails">
		<figure>
			<div class="clip"><Arena s={scene.moonwalker} thumb label="Moonwalker reversing towards B" /><span class="play">▶ clip</span></div>
			<figcaption>
				<strong>Moonwalker</strong> learned that driving backwards is the quickest way to a goal behind it. Its rays only
				look forward, so it reversed blind into walls. Fix: no reversing.
			</figcaption>
		</figure>
		<figure>
			<div class="clip"><Arena s={scene.scaredy} thumb label="Scaredy-Wheely frozen in the slalom" /><span class="play">▶ clip</span></div>
			<figcaption>
				<strong>Scaredy-Wheely</strong> was punished too hard for touching walls, so standing still became the
				safest choice. It froze in 1 in 4 empty arenas. Fix: a smaller penalty.
			</figcaption>
		</figure>
	</div>
	<p class="more"><a class="btn" href="#">Read the full write-up →</a></p>
</section>

<style>
	.story {
		margin-top: 56px;
	}
	h2 {
		margin: 0 0 14px;
		font-size: 24px;
	}
	h3 {
		margin: 36px 0 14px;
		font-size: 18px;
	}
	.cols {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr;
		gap: 32px;
		align-items: start;
	}
	.text p {
		margin: 0 0 12px;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	table {
		width: 100%;
		border-collapse: collapse;
		font-size: 13px;
	}
	caption {
		margin-bottom: 6px;
		text-align: left;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 12px;
	}
	th,
	td {
		padding: 5px 6px;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
		text-align: right;
	}
	thead th {
		font: 500 11px var(--font-mono);
		color: var(--muted);
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}
	tbody th {
		text-align: left;
		font-weight: 500;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}
	td {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	td.best {
		color: var(--fg);
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.fails {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 24px;
	}
	figure {
		margin: 0;
	}
	.clip {
		position: relative;
		overflow: hidden;
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
	}
	.play {
		position: absolute;
		right: 10px;
		bottom: 10px;
		padding: 2px 10px;
		border-radius: 999px;
		background: var(--fg);
		color: var(--bg);
		font-size: 12px;
	}
	figcaption {
		margin-top: 10px;
		font-size: 14px;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	figcaption strong {
		color: var(--fg);
	}
	.more {
		margin: 28px 0 0;
	}
	@media (max-width: 760px) {
		.cols,
		.fails {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
		table {
			font-size: 12px;
		}
		thead th {
			font-size: 9.5px;
			letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		}
		th,
		td {
			padding: 5px 3px;
		}
	}
</style>
